      "essence": "Clear boundaries, mediation, and timely withdrawal gives Conflict a path beyond force, passivity, or premature certainty.",
      "summary": "The Daoist lens attends to how force can accord with the configuration instead of contending with it. In Conflict, the central situation is divergent claims hardening into conflict, and the commentarial evidence repeatedly emphasizes contention, danger, and beneficial. The main danger is pursuing vindication beyond the useful limit, especially when partial conditions are mistaken for permission to press ahead. Its constructive capacity is clear boundaries, mediation, and timely withdrawal, expressed through attention to sequence, relation, and the limits of the present position. Transformation comes through responsive timing: capacity remains available because it is neither suppressed nor spent against the grain.",
